azul-icons-haiku: the Haiku project's icons, as HVIF

The .hvif files in icons/ are icons from the Haiku project's icon set,
https://github.com/haiku/haiku, folder data/artwork/icons, at the commit
60e29589f83123ca4cb8e9fdcc83951d217af1e5 (icons/UPSTREAM.txt lists every
file with its upstream git blob). They were converted from Icon-O-Matic's
documents to HVIF by tools/iom2hvif.py and are otherwise unchanged.

Haiku's data/artwork/ReadMe says of them: "Unless specified otherwise, the
other graphics (for example, cursors/*, icons/*, boot_splash/splash_icons*,
...,) are released under the MIT license." No icon used here specifies
otherwise. The trademarked Haiku logos are not among them.

tools/iom2hvif.py is a port of Haiku's MIT-licensed sources (Icon-O-Matic's
FlatIconExporter and the icon library's archive readers by Stephan Aßmus and
Zardshard, the BMessage formats of src/kits/app by Axel Dörfler and Michael
Lotz; Copyright Haiku, Inc.).

The icons and the ported code are distributed under the MIT License, as the
Haiku project ships it (data/system/data/licenses/MIT):


